{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011SqXVCzfBysuBQjYYfYsYM","type":"tool_result","content":"430\t### 9. MCP Surface\n431\t\n432\tThe MCP contract should expose high-level assistant workflows rather than forcing clients to compose low-level graph calls.\n433\t\n434\tRequired workflow tools:\n435\t\n436\t- `get_context_capsule`\n437\t- `prepare_change`\n438\t- `plan_edit`\n439\t- `trace_scenario`\n440\t- `diagnose_failure`\n441\t- `find_relevant_tests`\n442\t- `impact_from_diff`\n443\t- `get_docs_capsule`\n444\t- `get_backlinks`\n445\t- `expand_context`\n446\t- `get_working_set_context`\n447\t- `get_repo_playbook`\n448\t- `search_symbols`\n449\t- `search_memory`\n450\t- `record_workflow_outcome`\n451\t\n452\tNew or redesigned memory tools:\n453\t\n454\t- `get_task_memory`\n455\t- `save_memory`\n456\t- `propose_memory_evolution`\n457\t- `apply_memory_evolution`\n458\t- `verify_memory`\n459\t- `explain_memory`\n460\t- `list_memory_conflicts`\n461\t- `consolidate_session`\n462\t- `get_memory_metrics`\n463\t- `get_event_trace`\n464\t\n465\tTool surface discipline: ten new memory tools is a meaningful cognitive load for clients. Before shipping Phase 8, audit whether `propose_memory_evolution` + `apply_memory_evolution` can collapse into a single tool with an `action` parameter, and whether `verify_memory` + `explain_memory` can be unified. The goal is the smallest surface that covers all assistant workflows. Consolidate before stabilizing the MCP contract.\n466\t\n467\tEvery tool response should support:\n468\t\n469\t- compact rendering\n470\t- full structured JSON\n471\t- context handles\n472\t- stable expansion targets\n473\t- budget controls\n474\t- diagnostic explanations where useful\n475\t\n476\t### 10. Human Review Surface\n477\t\n478\tAgents are the primary client, but durable memory needs human inspectability.\n479\t\n480\tRequired operator views:\n481\t\n482\t- memory inbox\n483\t- proposed promotions\n484\t- proposed contradictions\n485\t- stale memory list\n486\t- memory evidence view\n487\t- event trace view\n488\t- retrieval explanation view\n489\t- usefulness metrics\n490\t- workspace graph health\n491\t- indexing health\n492\t- consolidation queue\n493\t\n494\tThis can be a VS Code extension panel or local web UI. It should be a review and trust surface, not the center of the product.\n495\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"589d9a30-530c-4e7c-8151-20cc70f1285a","uuid":"b0eae3b0-35a3-4d70-b8f6-1c003aa7e803","timestamp":"2026-05-17T14:40:00.867Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md","content":"### 9. MCP Surface\n\nThe MCP contract should expose high-level assistant workflows rather than forcing clients to compose low-level graph calls.\n\nRequired workflow tools:\n\n- `get_context_capsule`\n- `prepare_change`\n- `plan_edit`\n- `trace_scenario`\n- `diagnose_failure`\n- `find_relevant_tests`\n- `impact_from_diff`\n- `get_docs_capsule`\n- `get_backlinks`\n- `expand_context`\n- `get_working_set_context`\n- `get_repo_playbook`\n- `search_symbols`\n- `search_memory`\n- `record_workflow_outcome`\n\nNew or redesigned memory tools:\n\n- `get_task_memory`\n- `save_memory`\n- `propose_memory_evolution`\n- `apply_memory_evolution`\n- `verify_memory`\n- `explain_memory`\n- `list_memory_conflicts`\n- `consolidate_session`\n- `get_memory_metrics`\n- `get_event_trace`\n\nTool surface discipline: ten new memory tools is a meaningful cognitive load for clients. Before shipping Phase 8, audit whether `propose_memory_evolution` + `apply_memory_evolution` can collapse into a single tool with an `action` parameter, and whether `verify_memory` + `explain_memory` can be unified. The goal is the smallest surface that covers all assistant workflows. Consolidate before stabilizing the MCP contract.\n\nEvery tool response should support:\n\n- compact rendering\n- full structured JSON\n- context handles\n- stable expansion targets\n- budget controls\n- diagnostic explanations where useful\n\n### 10. Human Review Surface\n\nAgents are the primary client, but durable memory needs human inspectability.\n\nRequired operator views:\n\n- memory inbox\n- proposed promotions\n- proposed contradictions\n- stale memory list\n- memory evidence view\n- event trace view\n- retrieval explanation view\n- usefulness metrics\n- workspace graph health\n- indexing health\n- consolidation queue\n\nThis can be a VS Code extension panel or local web UI. It should be a review and trust surface, not the center of the product.\n","numLines":66,"startLine":430,"totalLines":969}}}
