{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BXJShxrTepCGqXTiPuJQTo","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# MCP Surface Audit\n2\t\n3\tThis audit is the Phase 8 contract check for the cognitive workspace fork. It reconciles the MCP surface in `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` with [## MCP Surface](../plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#mcp-surface), [## MCP Tool Contract Principles](../plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#mcp-tool-contract-principles), [## Phase 8: Workflow Engine V2](../plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-8-workflow-engine-v2), and the compatibility rules in [MCP Compatibility Policy](./2026-05-16-mcp-compatibility-policy.md). The canonical final inventory is [MCP Tool Reference](./2026-05-16-mcp-tool-reference.md).\n4\t\n5\tSpec framing from [## MCP Surface](../plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#mcp-surface):\n6\t\n7\t> Tool surface discipline: ten new memory tools is a meaningful cognitive load for clients. Before shipping Phase 8, audit whether `propose_memory_evolution` + `apply_memory_evolution` can collapse into a single tool with an `action` parameter, and whether `verify_memory` + `explain_memory` can be unified. The goal is the smallest surface that covers all assistant workflows. Consolidate before stabilizing the MCP contract.\n8\t\n9\t## Audit findings\n10\t\n11\tThe Phase 8 surface keeps the required workflow vocabulary stable, adds the memory tools that introduce new assistant workflows, and collapses nominal memory tools where separate names would only split one lifecycle operation across multiple verbs.\n12\t\n13\t| Decision | Rationale | Spec authorization | Shim policy | Shim-removal deadline |\n14\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n15\t| Collapse `propose_memory_evolution` and `apply_memory_evolution` into canonical `propose_memory_evolution` with `action` values `propose`, `apply`, and `reject`. | Proposal creation, application, and rejection are one auditable memory-evolution lifecycle. A single tool keeps proposal ids, decision reasons, actor metadata, and transactional update semantics in one contract. | [## MCP Surface](../plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#mcp-surface) says to audit whether the pair can collapse and sets the goal as the smallest surface that covers assistant workflows. | `apply_memory_evolution` remains advertised as a deprecated shim in `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/propose_memory_evolution.rs`; it forwards to `propose_memory_evolution(action=\"apply\")` and attaches `deprecation_warning`. | Remove no earlier than one full numbered phase cycle after Phase 8 once first-party prompts, fixtures, docs, and cached examples call the canonical action form, following [## Shim removal protocol](./2026-05-16-mcp-compatibility-policy.md#shim-removal-protocol). |\n16\t| Collapse `verify_memory` and `explain_memory` into canonical `verify_explain_memory` with `mode` values `verify`, `explain`, and `verify_and_explain`. | Verification and explanation share the same evidence checks, status taxonomy, confidence delta, and expansion handle. Keeping two canonical tools would duplicate result semantics and make clients choose between freshness and diagnostics. | [## MCP Surface](../plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#mcp-surface) explicitly asks whether `verify_memory` and `explain_memory` can be unified. [## MCP Tool Contract Principles](../plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#mcp-tool-contract-principles) requires memory-bearing responses to identify evidence strength, verification status, freshness, and explanation metadata. | `verify_memory` and `explain_memory` remain advertised deprecated shims in `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/verify_explain_memory.rs`; each forces the appropriate `mode` and attaches `deprecation_warning`. | Remove no earlier than one full numbered phase cycle after Phase 8 once maintained clients have migrated to `verify_explain_memory`, following [## Shim removal protocol](./2026-05-16-mcp-compatibility-policy.md#shim-removal-protocol). |\n17\t| No further Phase 8 collapses. | Review of `workflow_v2/`, `memory_v2/`, and `handle_tools_call` found no additional adjacent tools that merely expose modes of one lifecycle. Existing pairs that look similar operate on different identities, evidence sources, or user intents. | [## MCP Surface](../plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#mcp-surface) requires consolidation before stabilizing the MCP contract, not name reduction at the cost of assistant ergonomics. | Existing legacy aliases from [## Legacy aliases and deadlines](./2026-05-16-mcp-compatibility-policy.md#legacy-aliases-and-deadlines) remain callable-only compatibility shims; they are not reintroduced as advertised canonical names. | Existing alias deadlines remain governed by the T02 policy: one full phase cycle after canonical migration, updated docs and fixtures, and compatibility test coverage. |\n18\t\n19\t## Collapsed tools\n20\t\n21\t| Spec-nominal tool | Actual implementation | Implementing file | Status |\n22\t|---|---|---|---|\n23\t| `propose_memory_evolution` | `propose_memory_evolution(action=\"propose\")` | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/propose_memory_evolution.rs` | Canonical. |\n24\t| `apply_memory_evolution` | `propose_memory_evolution(action=\"apply\")` | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/propose_memory_evolution.rs` | Deprecated advertised shim with warning. |\n25\t| `verify_memory` | `verify_explain_memory(mode=\"verify\")` | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/verify_explain_memory.rs` | Deprecated advertised shim with warning. |\n26\t| `explain_memory` | `verify_explain_memory(mode=\"explain\")` | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/verify_explain_memory.rs` | Deprecated advertised shim with warning. |\n27\t\n28\t## Decisions not to collapse\n29\t\n30\t| Considered pair or group | Decision | Rationale |\n31\t|---|---|---|\n32\t| `get_context_capsule` and `get_docs_capsule` | Keep separate. | `get_context_capsule` anchors source-code pivots, symbols, tests, and nearby implementation context. `get_docs_capsule` anchors Markdown docs, sections, and code mentions. Combining them would force every discovery call to carry both source and docs ranking controls. |\n33\t| `get_backlinks`, `get_outgoing_links`, and `find_stale_docs` | Keep separate. | Backlinks answer inbound references, outgoing links answer outbound references, and stale-doc detection compares changed files or symbols against docs. They share graph substrate but expose different traversal directions and review intents. |\n34\t| `prepare_change` and `plan_edit` | Keep separate. | `prepare_change` is a first workflow tool for fix/add/refactor tasks once the area is known. `plan_edit` is patch-oriented and returns edit spans, affected callers, docs, and tests. Collapsing them would hide the distinction between change preparation and concrete edit planning. |\n35\t| `trace_scenario` and `diagnose_failure` | Keep separate. | `diagnose_failure` starts from compiler/test/runtime failure text. `trace_scenario` starts from behavioral descriptions and traces likely execution paths. Their inputs, diagnostics, and ranking signals differ. |\n36\t| `get_task_memory`, `search_memory`, and legacy `get_session_context` | Keep separate for now. | `get_task_memory` is task-scoped and working-memory-aware. `search_memory` is a required query workflow over stored memories. `get_session_context` is a legacy session-recall contract classified as `redesigned-with-shim` in the T02 policy. Collapsing them now would create a backward-incompatible request shape. |\n37\t| `consolidate_session` and `propose_memory_evolution` | Keep separate. | `consolidate_session` produces proposal ids from event episodes and consolidation categories; `propose_memory_evolution` applies or rejects specific memory-evolution proposals. Generation and decision remain distinct workflow boundaries for auditability. |\n38\t| `get_memory_metrics`, `get_event_trace`, and `get_session_metrics` | Keep separate. | `get_memory_metrics` reports Phase 9 memory/workflow signals with provenance, `get_event_trace` pages event envelopes, and `get_session_metrics` reports live assistant-session MCP metrics. They have different scopes, budgets, and response shapes. |\n39\t| `inspect_working_memory` and `get_working_set_context` | Keep separate. | `inspect_working_memory` reads task working-memory checkpoints. `get_working_set_context` compresses already-known files and symbols into a code/docs/test bundle. The identity type and operator question are different. |\n40\t\n41\t## Reconciliation\n42\t\n43\tThe final advertised `tools/list` surface after Phase 8 contains the existing canonical workflow, graph, doc, memory, setup, and metrics tools plus ten Phase 8 memory entries, three of which are deprecated shims required for compatibility. `handle_tools_call` also accepts five callable-only legacy aliases from the T02 compatibility policy: `query_context`, `blast_radius`, `get_file_context`, `store_memory`, and `recall_memories`.\n44\t\n45\tThe required [## MCP Surface](../plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#mcp-surface) workflow tools are all present in [## Final tool list](./2026-05-16-mcp-tool-reference.md#final-tool-list): `get_context_capsule`, `prepare_change`, `plan_edit`, `trace_scenario`, `diagnose_failure`, `find_relevant_tests`, `impact_from_diff`, `get_docs_capsule`, `get_backlinks`, `expand_context`, `get_working_set_context`, `get_repo_playbook`, `search_symbols`, `search_memory`, and `record_workflow_outcome`.\n46\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"589d9a30-530c-4e7c-8151-20cc70f1285a","uuid":"2072213f-ebbd-4f76-9fb5-61d0e5c64ceb","timestamp":"2026-05-17T14:40:19.604Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-surface-audit.md","content":"# MCP Surface Audit\n\nThis audit is the Phase 8 contract check for the cognitive workspace fork. It reconciles the MCP surface in `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` with [## MCP Surface](../plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#mcp-surface), [## MCP Tool Contract Principles](../plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#mcp-tool-contract-principles), [## Phase 8: Workflow Engine V2](../plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-8-workflow-engine-v2), and the compatibility rules in [MCP Compatibility Policy](./2026-05-16-mcp-compatibility-policy.md). The canonical final inventory is [MCP Tool Reference](./2026-05-16-mcp-tool-reference.md).\n\nSpec framing from [## MCP Surface](../plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#mcp-surface):\n\n> Tool surface discipline: ten new memory tools is a meaningful cognitive load for clients. Before shipping Phase 8, audit whether `propose_memory_evolution` + `apply_memory_evolution` can collapse into a single tool with an `action` parameter, and whether `verify_memory` + `explain_memory` can be unified. The goal is the smallest surface that covers all assistant workflows. Consolidate before stabilizing the MCP contract.\n\n## Audit findings\n\nThe Phase 8 surface keeps the required workflow vocabulary stable, adds the memory tools that introduce new assistant workflows, and collapses nominal memory tools where separate names would only split one lifecycle operation across multiple verbs.\n\n| Decision | Rationale | Spec authorization | Shim policy | Shim-removal deadline |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Collapse `propose_memory_evolution` and `apply_memory_evolution` into canonical `propose_memory_evolution` with `action` values `propose`, `apply`, and `reject`. | Proposal creation, application, and rejection are one auditable memory-evolution lifecycle. A single tool keeps proposal ids, decision reasons, actor metadata, and transactional update semantics in one contract. | [## MCP Surface](../plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#mcp-surface) says to audit whether the pair can collapse and sets the goal as the smallest surface that covers assistant workflows. | `apply_memory_evolution` remains advertised as a deprecated shim in `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/propose_memory_evolution.rs`; it forwards to `propose_memory_evolution(action=\"apply\")` and attaches `deprecation_warning`. | Remove no earlier than one full numbered phase cycle after Phase 8 once first-party prompts, fixtures, docs, and cached examples call the canonical action form, following [## Shim removal protocol](./2026-05-16-mcp-compatibility-policy.md#shim-removal-protocol). |\n| Collapse `verify_memory` and `explain_memory` into canonical `verify_explain_memory` with `mode` values `verify`, `explain`, and `verify_and_explain`. | Verification and explanation share the same evidence checks, status taxonomy, confidence delta, and expansion handle. Keeping two canonical tools would duplicate result semantics and make clients choose between freshness and diagnostics. | [## MCP Surface](../plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#mcp-surface) explicitly asks whether `verify_memory` and `explain_memory` can be unified. [## MCP Tool Contract Principles](../plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#mcp-tool-contract-principles) requires memory-bearing responses to identify evidence strength, verification status, freshness, and explanation metadata. | `verify_memory` and `explain_memory` remain advertised deprecated shims in `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/verify_explain_memory.rs`; each forces the appropriate `mode` and attaches `deprecation_warning`. | Remove no earlier than one full numbered phase cycle after Phase 8 once maintained clients have migrated to `verify_explain_memory`, following [## Shim removal protocol](./2026-05-16-mcp-compatibility-policy.md#shim-removal-protocol). |\n| No further Phase 8 collapses. | Review of `workflow_v2/`, `memory_v2/`, and `handle_tools_call` found no additional adjacent tools that merely expose modes of one lifecycle. Existing pairs that look similar operate on different identities, evidence sources, or user intents. | [## MCP Surface](../plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#mcp-surface) requires consolidation before stabilizing the MCP contract, not name reduction at the cost of assistant ergonomics. | Existing legacy aliases from [## Legacy aliases and deadlines](./2026-05-16-mcp-compatibility-policy.md#legacy-aliases-and-deadlines) remain callable-only compatibility shims; they are not reintroduced as advertised canonical names. | Existing alias deadlines remain governed by the T02 policy: one full phase cycle after canonical migration, updated docs and fixtures, and compatibility test coverage. |\n\n## Collapsed tools\n\n| Spec-nominal tool | Actual implementation | Implementing file | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `propose_memory_evolution` | `propose_memory_evolution(action=\"propose\")` | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/propose_memory_evolution.rs` | Canonical. |\n| `apply_memory_evolution` | `propose_memory_evolution(action=\"apply\")` | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/propose_memory_evolution.rs` | Deprecated advertised shim with warning. |\n| `verify_memory` | `verify_explain_memory(mode=\"verify\")` | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/verify_explain_memory.rs` | Deprecated advertised shim with warning. |\n| `explain_memory` | `verify_explain_memory(mode=\"explain\")` | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/verify_explain_memory.rs` | Deprecated advertised shim with warning. |\n\n## Decisions not to collapse\n\n| Considered pair or group | Decision | Rationale |\n|---|---|---|\n| `get_context_capsule` and `get_docs_capsule` | Keep separate. | `get_context_capsule` anchors source-code pivots, symbols, tests, and nearby implementation context. `get_docs_capsule` anchors Markdown docs, sections, and code mentions. Combining them would force every discovery call to carry both source and docs ranking controls. |\n| `get_backlinks`, `get_outgoing_links`, and `find_stale_docs` | Keep separate. | Backlinks answer inbound references, outgoing links answer outbound references, and stale-doc detection compares changed files or symbols against docs. They share graph substrate but expose different traversal directions and review intents. |\n| `prepare_change` and `plan_edit` | Keep separate. | `prepare_change` is a first workflow tool for fix/add/refactor tasks once the area is known. `plan_edit` is patch-oriented and returns edit spans, affected callers, docs, and tests. Collapsing them would hide the distinction between change preparation and concrete edit planning. |\n| `trace_scenario` and `diagnose_failure` | Keep separate. | `diagnose_failure` starts from compiler/test/runtime failure text. `trace_scenario` starts from behavioral descriptions and traces likely execution paths. Their inputs, diagnostics, and ranking signals differ. |\n| `get_task_memory`, `search_memory`, and legacy `get_session_context` | Keep separate for now. | `get_task_memory` is task-scoped and working-memory-aware. `search_memory` is a required query workflow over stored memories. `get_session_context` is a legacy session-recall contract classified as `redesigned-with-shim` in the T02 policy. Collapsing them now would create a backward-incompatible request shape. |\n| `consolidate_session` and `propose_memory_evolution` | Keep separate. | `consolidate_session` produces proposal ids from event episodes and consolidation categories; `propose_memory_evolution` applies or rejects specific memory-evolution proposals. Generation and decision remain distinct workflow boundaries for auditability. |\n| `get_memory_metrics`, `get_event_trace`, and `get_session_metrics` | Keep separate. | `get_memory_metrics` reports Phase 9 memory/workflow signals with provenance, `get_event_trace` pages event envelopes, and `get_session_metrics` reports live assistant-session MCP metrics. They have different scopes, budgets, and response shapes. |\n| `inspect_working_memory` and `get_working_set_context` | Keep separate. | `inspect_working_memory` reads task working-memory checkpoints. `get_working_set_context` compresses already-known files and symbols into a code/docs/test bundle. The identity type and operator question are different. |\n\n## Reconciliation\n\nThe final advertised `tools/list` surface after Phase 8 contains the existing canonical workflow, graph, doc, memory, setup, and metrics tools plus ten Phase 8 memory entries, three of which are deprecated shims required for compatibility. `handle_tools_call` also accepts five callable-only legacy aliases from the T02 compatibility policy: `query_context`, `blast_radius`, `get_file_context`, `store_memory`, and `recall_memories`.\n\nThe required [## MCP Surface](../plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#mcp-surface) workflow tools are all present in [## Final tool list](./2026-05-16-mcp-tool-reference.md#final-tool-list): `get_context_capsule`, `prepare_change`, `plan_edit`, `trace_scenario`, `diagnose_failure`, `find_relevant_tests`, `impact_from_diff`, `get_docs_capsule`, `get_backlinks`, `expand_context`, `get_working_set_context`, `get_repo_playbook`, `search_symbols`, `search_memory`, and `record_workflow_outcome`.\n","numLines":46,"startLine":1,"totalLines":46}}}
