{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XYbtLw6VAXw32i49stvoKe","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# MCP Compatibility Policy\n2\t\n3\t## Summary\n4\t\n5\tThis policy defines the Phase 0 compatibility contract required by [docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-0-fork-foundation](../plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-0-fork-foundation). It classifies the current MCP surface implemented in `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` and binds later redesigns to the stability rules in [## MCP Surface](../plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#mcp-surface) and [## MCP Tool Contract Principles](../plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#mcp-tool-contract-principles).\n6\t\n7\tThis policy applies to the in-place successor architecture described in [docs/architecture/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-architecture.md](./2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-architecture.md).\n8\t\n9\t## Status classes\n10\t\n11\t| Status | Meaning |\n12\t|---|---|\n13\t| `stable` | No breaking request or response change is planned. Existing fields remain valid; only behavior fixes are allowed. |\n14\t| `additive` | The tool keeps its request and response contract, but may gain optional response fields, richer metadata, or stable identity fields. |\n15\t| `redesigned-with-shim` | A successor contract is planned. The legacy tool name must keep working through a compatibility adapter for at least one full phase cycle. |\n16\t| `deprecated-with-deadline` | The name is already a legacy alias. It remains callable only through the documented shim window and should be removed after the deadline protocol is satisfied. |\n17\t\n18\t## Canonical tool inventory\n19\t\n20\tThe current canonical `tools/list` surface contains 37 tools. Their successor classification is:\n21\t\n22\t| Tool | Status | Successor expectation |\n23\t|---|---|---|\n24\t| `get_context_capsule` | `additive` | Core workflow remains; Phase 8 may add event and memory reasons, stable identity payloads, and richer diagnostics. |\n25\t| `prepare_change` | `additive` | Core workflow remains; later phases add event-backed retrieval, memory evidence, and working-memory details. |\n26\t| `plan_edit` | `additive` | Core workflow remains; later phases add shared identity, event, and memory context. |\n27\t| `trace_scenario` | `additive` | Core workflow remains; later phases add event episodes and verification signals. |\n28\t| `find_relevant_tests` | `additive` | Stable name; later phases add graph/event-backed confidence and identity fields. |\n29\t| `impact_from_diff` | `additive` | Stable name; later phases add identity-rich impact edges and event-derived co-change signals. |\n30\t| `get_working_set_context` | `additive` | Stable name; later phases may enrich output with explicit working-memory checkpoint metadata. |\n31\t| `summarize_subsystem` | `additive` | Stable name; later phases add memory and event explanations. |\n32\t| `get_repo_playbook` | `additive` | Stable name; later phases add consolidated procedures and evidence provenance. |\n33\t| `get_docs_capsule` | `additive` | Stable name; later phases add doc identity, stale-against signals, and event evidence. |\n34\t| `get_backlinks` | `additive` | Stable name; later phases add typed identity outputs and verification hints. |\n35\t| `get_outgoing_links` | `additive` | Stable name; later phases add typed identity outputs and verification hints. |\n36\t| `find_stale_docs` | `additive` | Stable name; later phases add verification jobs and stale evidence payloads. |\n37\t| `diagnose_failure` | `additive` | Stable name; later phases add event episodes, failure-pattern memory, and stronger diagnostics. |\n38\t| `record_workflow_outcome` | `additive` | Stable name; later phases add explicit event ids, memory ids, and proposal metadata. |\n39\t| `expand_context` | `additive` | Stable name; later phases add cross-substrate expansion targets over unified identities. |\n40\t| `get_symbol` | `additive` | Stable name; later phases add typed ids and richer evidence links. |\n41\t| `get_dependents` | `additive` | Stable name; later phases add typed ids and graph provenance. |\n42\t| `get_dependencies` | `additive` | Stable name; later phases add typed ids and graph provenance. |\n43\t| `get_impact_graph` | `additive` | Stable name; later phases add event-derived and verification-derived edges. |\n44\t| `search_symbols` | `additive` | Stable name; later phases add typed ids and ranking explanations. |\n45\t| `get_skeleton` | `additive` | Stable name; later phases add typed ids and richer structural metadata. |\n46\t| `save_observation` | `redesigned-with-shim` | Legacy observation-centric write path evolves toward `save_memory` over the broader memory class model. |\n47\t| `get_session_context` | `redesigned-with-shim` | Session-only memory recall evolves toward task-scoped and working-memory-aware retrieval such as `get_task_memory`. |\n48\t| `search_memory` | `additive` | Stable name; remains a required workflow tool but gains typed memory, evidence, and event-aware ranking fields. |\n49\t| `search_logic_flow` | `additive` | Stable name; later phases add typed ids and explainable path reasons. |\n50\t| `submit_lsp_edges` | `stable` | Internal graph enrichment contract stays narrow; no redesign is planned in the cognitive workspace phases. |\n51\t| `workspace_setup` | `stable` | Workspace convention summary remains stable; only content freshness changes are expected. |\n52\t| `index_status` | `stable` | Operational status tool remains stable; output may gain optional fields only if needed. |\n53\t| `get_session_metrics` | `additive` | Stable name; later phases add event-log and memory-usefulness metrics. |\n54\t| `get_project_rules` | `stable` | Project-rule summary remains stable; only content freshness changes are expected. |\n55\t| `list_observations` | `redesigned-with-shim` | Observation-centric listing evolves toward typ